
ewmseedarchiver:

Read MSEED messages from an Earthworm transport ring and write the 
miniSEED records to the file system in flexible file layout.

See the ewmseedarchiver.d file for further description of options.

Periodic archive synchronization
--------------------------------

Version 0.3.2 adds periodic synchronization of every open archive file.
Previously, continuously active files could remain open until a stream or
UTC-day change, so file data and file-size metadata might not become visible
to other processes promptly.  The module now calls fsync() on Unix and
_commit() on Windows once every hour by default.

The synchronization interval is controlled with the optional FlushInterval
command.  The value is specified in seconds:

  FlushInterval 3600

The default is 3600 seconds (one hour).  A value of 0 disables periodic
synchronization.  Negative values are rejected during configuration.

FlushInterval does not change the archive file name and does not split a
daily file.  To create a separate file for every hour, include the defining
hour flag, %H, in the Archive path.  For example on Windows:

  Archive D:\data\archive\%n\%s\%Y.%j.%H.%n.%s.%l.%c.mseed

With a daily Archive path and FlushInterval 3600, data continues to be
appended to the same daily file but is synchronized at least once per hour.
With %H in the path, a new file is selected for each hour based on the UTC
start time in each MiniSEED record.
